  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Riviera is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Anyone who wants a Skyliner ride to EPCOT or Hollywood Studios.</strong> The station is at the resort, and the ride to EPCOT's International Gateway is direct.</li>
      <li><strong>Couples who can live in a smaller room, or families who need a studio that sleeps five.</strong> A Tower Studio is built for two. A Deluxe Studio adds a queen bed and a single pull-down.</li>
      <li><strong>People who want character breakfast and a Signature dinner in the same rooftop restaurant.</strong> Topolino's Terrace does both, and the dinner does not include characters.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You need a standard hotel room rather than a villa-style studio.</strong> This is a Deluxe Villa resort. Even the smallest rooms use a pull-down bed, and the cash rates are in Deluxe territory.</li>
      <li><strong>Magic Kingdom is your main park.</strong> That trip is a bus, not a Skyliner or monorail.</li>
      <li><strong>You are staying the week of January 24 through 30, 2027, and the Skyliner was the reason you booked here.</strong> Official pages say the Skyliner will close that week for refurbishment, with buses running instead.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: who you think this resort is really for, from your own stays. Two or three sentences.]</span>
  </section>

