  <section id="booking">
    <h2>Booking and value tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Start with a Tower Studio if there are only two of you and you can live with a pull-down bed.</strong> In 2026 those rooms ran from $519 to $966 a night at full cash price including tax, depending on dates. That is the lowest cash rate at this resort.</li>
      <li><strong>Book a Deluxe Studio if you need to sleep more than two, or if you want a traditional bed in the room.</strong> Resort View studios ran about $742 to $1,290. Preferred View costs more and looks at the courtyard, the lake, the pool or the Skyliner.</li>
      <li><strong>This is also a Disney Vacation Club resort.</strong> Some guests stay here on points or by renting points, which can change the value math. We are quoting cash rates in this guide.</li>
      <li><strong>If you are staying the last week of January 2027, plan on buses instead of the Skyliner.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Check Disney's own offers page first.</strong> Disney points to <a href="https://disneyworld.disney.go.com/special-offers/">its special offers page</a> for discounts. Our deals hub will track current ones.</li>
      <li><strong>Lightning Lane head start:</strong> Disney resort guests can buy Lightning Lane passes up to 7 days before their stay.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="fg-callout">
